<title>GERMANY: W.German Aug industry output rises 0.3 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>W.German Aug industry output rises 0.3 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Aug 96    July 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +0.3	 +1.4	 -2.7</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +2.1	 -0.9	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		96.8	 96.5	 94.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Aug 96		 July 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining		     85.2	  -0.5    85.6	  -2.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   96.5	  +1.3    95.3	  +0.8</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods  100.5	  +2.3    98.2	  +0.6</p>
<p>	Capital goods     94.5	  -0.9    95.4	  +2.1</p>
<p>	Consumer durables 91.6	  +5.8    86.6	  +2.5</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    92.5	  +0.1    92.4	  -1.6</p>
<p> Energy output	   111.7	  +1.5   110.0	  +0.4</p>
<p> Construction	     91.5	 -10.6   102.3	  +9.2</p>
<p>Two month comparison July/Aug 96 with May/June 96:</p>
<p>    Industrial production	    +2.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison July/Aug 96 with July/Aug 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output			+0.9</p>
<p> Mining				     -6.7</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		  +1.8</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods	+1.2</p>
<p>		Capital goods	     +3.6</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	 +8.9</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	    -1.6</p>
<p> Energy output			    +5.8</p>
<p> Construction			     -8.2</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
